  "raw_text": "n you have time constraints and are usually alone. How does price change your choice? For example, if your Wendy's single cost two dollars more, what would you do? User: I would pay the two dollars more because that is worth it. Agent: Understood. You would pay the two dollars more because you feel it's worth it. Now, if there was a deal, what would you do differently? User: If there was a deal I would probably order it to save money. Agent: Okay, you'd order it to save money if there was a deal. Let's shift gears a bit. Over the past two weeks, what are your most common fast-food patterns? This includes when you eat it, what you usually order, and what typically triggers it. User: I usually drive through for breakfast, it's convenient on the way to work and sometimes if I have a short lunch and a fast food restaurant is convenient to running errands I will use that. Agent: Thank you for sharing your typical fast-food patterns, Nicole. Now, what does \"good value\" mean to you in fas",
